  "body": "Stacked on #4096. The branch contains the #4096 commits (now at `d36523d9d`, with its review fixes) merged in. The own commits of this PR are `f2eedafa0` (the spindle slice) and `808743798` (the fixes of the #4119 review); `61e0f593e` merges the #4096 review fixes, with no change to the #3643 code.\n\n## What changed\n\nThis PR is the spindle slice of #3643. It is pure domain code in `camcraft-tools`. It adds no crate edge, no ECS code and no file I/O.\n\n- `frame.rs`: a checked rigid frame (origin, unit Z, unit X). It composes a local frame onto a parent, turns about its own Z and moves along it. A non-finite or degenerate frame is refused by name.\n- `component_geometry.rs`: the port frames, the cutting point, the revolved body and the bore stops of one #3642 component, in the component's own frame. The origin is the machine side (MCS) and +Z points to the machine. `ComponentGeometry::with_stop(port, depth)` states a bore stop. `ComponentGeometry::holder` makes a built-in library holder a component with the entry's own outline. It states no bore stop, because the library has no bore depth.\n- `tool_assembly.rs`, `tool_assembly_body.rs`, `tool_assembly_error.rs`: the resolver. The root MCS is the identity. Each child MCS sits on its parent's port, turned by `z_rot_deg` and, on a plain or Weldon bore, moved to `projection_mm` or to the stated bore stop. The result is moved so that the cutting tip is the origin of the tool frame. It gives:\n  - the gauge length (the root MCS above the tip);\n  - the cutting diameter and corner radius (the solid tool's own values, or the insert's values from its seat point and nose);\n  - the judged `HolderProfile` that the collision laws read today, plus a drawn `SpunProfile` of it.\n- Refusals by name: the #3642 fit errors (`check_fit`), a missing frame, an ambiguous or taken port, a cycle, a bad parent, two roots, no cutter or two cutters, a non-finite turn or stickout, a stickout that is not on a plain or Weldon bore, a shank with no stickout and no stated bore stop, a bore stop as deep as the tool, a stickout that pushes the shank past the bore stop, an off-axis body, a body below the tip or past the size caps, and a body in the flutes.\n- `docs/decisions/3643-tool-assemblies.md` records the frame convention, the stickout rule, the body union and what is left.\n\n## Readings\n\n- One body is judged exactly as `app::tool_body::build_library` judges a library holder: `SpunProfile::holder_profile()` of its outline at its place.\n- Several bodies are united band by band. The larger radius wins where two bodies overlap. A span that no body covers takes the smaller radius of its neighbours, so the bands stay contiguous.\n- The stop rule: a shank has a home position only on a stated stop. The nose face is never a home position. There the whole tool hangs out of the bore, the gauge length is too long by the insertion depth, and the holder body is too far from the tip. A shank mount with no stickout and no stated stop is refused by name.\n- The flute check is the same `HolderProfile::enclose` test that `app::tool_body::fits` uses.\n\n## Pinning tests (`camcraft-tools` lib, `tool_assembly_tests`)\n\n- `a_collet_chuck_assembly_is_judged_as_the_library_holder`: the equivalence pin. A BT30 ER20 chuck, an ER20 collet and an end mill at a stickout give the same gauge length and the same bands (within 1e-9 mm) as today's `HolderRef` for the same numbers.\n- `a_weldon_holder_with_the_shank_home_is_judged_as_the_library_holder`: the same pin for a BT40 Weldon 12 mm holder with a stated bore stop. The true stickout is the tool length less the stop depth. The shank home on the stop and the same stickout stated give the same gauge length and bands as `HolderRef` at that stickout.\n- `a_shank_with_no_stated_stop_or_past_its_stop_is_refused`: no stickout and no stop (a library holder and a plain bore), a stop as deep as the tool, and a stickout past the stop are refused by name. A shallower shank is legal. `with_stop` refuses an unknown port and a depth of 0, below 0 or NaN.\n- `overlapping_bodies_keep_the_larger_radius`: an ER collet body that reaches 20 mm into the chuck nose. The chuck radius stays in the overlap.\n- `a_gap_between_bodies_takes_the_smaller_neighbour`: a 30 mm span with no body between two bodies takes the smaller neighbour radius, not 0.\n- `a_stack_up_sums_its_lengths_and_unites_its_bodies`: adapter + holder + tool. The lengths sum, each MCS frame is in its place, and the two bodies are united.\n- `an_indexable_cutter_takes_its_diameter_and_corner_from_seat_and_insert`: a CC seat 12.5 mm off the axis and a CCMT09T304 insert give Ø25 and r0.4, at three `z_rot_deg` values.\n- `a_wrong_insert_or_a_missing_seat_is_refused_by_the_fit_checks`: shape, port and coupling refusals of #3642.\n- `links_frames_and_transforms_are_refused_by_name`, `bodies_in_the_flutes_and_bad_stickouts_are_refused_by_name`, `an_off_axis_body_and_degenerate_geometry_are_refused_by_name`.\n\n## Mutations (`cargo test -p camcraft-tools --lib tool_assembly`, on `808743798`)\n\n| Mutation | Result |\n|---|---|\n| none (base) | 11 passed |\n| union: overlap takes `f64::min` | caught by `overlapping_bodies_keep_the_larger_radius` |\n| union: a gap gets radius `0.0` | caught by `a_gap_between_bodies_takes_the_smaller_neighbour` |\n| no stop: the shank sits on the nose face (the old default) | caught by `a_shank_with_no_stated_stop_or_past_its_stop_is_refused` |\n| the past-the-stop check removed | caught by `a_shank_with_no_stated_stop_or_past_its_stop_is_refused` |\n\n## Gate (Windows build lane, `winbuild`)\n\n- Head `808743798` (the #4119 review fixes):\n  - `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: one step, `tools suites: lib`: 176 passed, 0 failed.\n  - `cargo clippy -p camcraft-tools --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n  - Light lane: not run again. The fixes change only `camcraft-tools` lib code and the decision file.\n- Head `61e0f593e` (after the merge of the #4096 review fixes):\n  - `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: one step, `tools suites: lib`: 173 passed, 0 failed.\n  - `cargo clippy -p camcraft-tools --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- Head `f2eedafa0` (the slice before that merge), gated on a trial merge with origin/main:\n  - `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: `tools suites: lib` ok, 0 failed.\n  - `cargo xtask gate light`: 6 of 6 steps ok, 0 failed, 0 stalled.\n  - `cargo clippy -p camcraft-tools --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- P6: no heavy step. No toolpath, simulation or post code changed.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No caller reads the resolver yet. No toolpath, simulation or post code changed, so the `example_catalog*` suites do not apply.\n- The first tests were written with the code. The review fixes were checked by the mutations above.\n\n## Left for later issues\n\n- #3643 (the rest): the lathe side (`LatheClearance`, turning orientation 1-8, the CRP of a turning insert, `MAX_TIP_GAP`), STEP/STL/OBJ mesh bodies, `MCS_INSERT` as `CsysRole::Mounting`, and `crates/app/src/tool_assembly.rs`.\n- #3644: store the components and their geometry on the document, and make `ToolBody` from `AssemblyBody` (`build_spun` takes the `spun` outline; the judged `profile` is the same).\n- #3645: persist `ComponentGeometry`. `ComponentGeometry::holder` already makes a built-in holder a component.\n- #3646: multi-seat cutters and a full `Tool` record (kind, flutes, axial depth) for an indexable cutter. This slice gives the diameter and the corner radius only.\n\nChangelog: none (no user-facing behaviour yet; the resolver has no caller).\n\nEffort: high\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nRefs #3643\n\n",
